顯示美國購物中心復甦不平衡"},{"title":"Simon Property Group Q3 FFO Falls, Revenue Rises; 2026 FFO Guidance Raised","src":"www.marketscreener.com","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwwFBVV95cUxQRlJZTjRnQVJ3ZjV0MXJnV1p5aWljNDEwZFhobURFX1lXTmo3eFVnWVFuLXV3cXg5Q3JkZnhvQVhhbm1JMzZpczA5MmdmSlRpWlg4WkRHV0lnS2ZJQl9BczF0cW5FVXdmWGRHd01ucmRQZDFGUXpJNDJkNlRxTXZreTVkRnhTUHFHQXI3WHFnb2Q3WVJ0T1B3SUZtVkpxdkFrR1VmVUtVM180ODlQWV90OG8wdXk4eTc1TU56eVNMQU9HVFE?oc=5","date":"2026-11-05","zh":"西蒙地產集團第三季​​ FFO 下降，收入上升；提出 2026 年 FFO 指導意見"}],"themes":[{"name":"財報","count":14},{"name":"股票回購/股利","count":2},{"name":"訂單/合約","count":1}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-02-25","period":"2025-12-31","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1063761/000110465926019419/spg-20251231x10k.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"Simon Property Group, Inc. is an Indiana corporation that operates as a self-administered and self-managed real estate investment trust, or REIT, under the Internal Revenue Code of 1986, as amended, or the Internal Revenue Code. REITs will generally not be liable for U.S. federal corporate income taxes as long as they distribute not less than 100% of their REIT taxable income. Simon Property Group, L.P. is our majority-owned Indiana partnership subsidiary that owns directly or indirectly all of our real estate properties and other assets. Unless stated otherwise or the context otherwise requires, references to \"Simon\" mean Simon Property Group, Inc. and references to the \"Operating Partnership\" mean Simon Property Group, L.P. References to \"we,\" \"us\" and \"our\" mean collectively Simon, the Operating Partnership and those entities/subsidiaries owned or controlled by Simon and/or the Operat","zh":"Simon Property Group, Inc. 是一家印第安納州公司，根據 1986 年《國內稅收法》（經修訂）或《國內稅收法》作為自我管理和自我管理的房地產投資信託基金 (REIT) 運營。只要 REIT 分配不少於 100% 的 REIT 應稅收入，則通常無需繳納美國聯邦企業所得稅。 Simon Property Group, L.P. 是我們在印第安納州擁有多數股權的合夥子公司，直接或間接擁有我們所有的房地產和其他資產。除非另有說明或上下文另有要求，否則提及的「西蒙」是指 Simon Property Group, Inc.，提及的「營運合夥企業」是指 Simon Property Group, L.P. 提及的「我們」、「我們」和「我們的」統指西蒙、營運合夥企業以及西蒙和/或營運商擁有或控制的實體/子公司。"},{"en":"We own, develop and manage premier shopping, dining, entertainment and mixed-use destinations, which consist primarily of malls, Premium Outlets , and The Mills . As of December 31, 2025, we owned or held an interest in 212 income-producing properties in the United States, which consisted of 108 malls, 70 Premium Outlets, 16 Mills, six lifestyle centers, and 12 other retail properties in 38 states and Puerto Rico. Internationally, as of December 31, 2025, we had ownership interests in 42 properties primarily located in Asia, Europe and Canada. As of December 31, 2025, we also owned a 22.2% equity stake in Kl pierre SA, or Kl pierre, a publicly traded, Paris-based real estate company, which owns, or has an interest in, shopping centers located in 13 countries in Europe. We also have interests in investments in retail operations (such as Catalyst Brands LLC); an e-commerce venture (Rue Gil","zh":"我們擁有、開發和管理一流的購物、餐飲、娛樂和綜合用途目的地，其中主要包括購物中心、Premium Outlets 和 The Mills。截至 2025 年 12 月 31 日，我們在美國擁有或持有 212 個創收物業的權益，其中包括 108 個購物中心、70 個高級奧特萊斯、16 個磨坊、6 個生活中心以及分佈在 38 個州和波多黎各的 12 個其他零售物業。在國際上，截至 2025 年 12 月 31 日，我們擁有主要位於亞洲、歐洲和加拿大的 42 處房產的所有權權益。截至 2025 年 12 月 31 日，我們還擁有 Kl pierre SA 或 Kl pierre 22.2% 的股權，Kl pierre 是一家總部位於巴黎的上市房地產公司，該公司在歐洲 13 個國家擁有或擁有購物中心的權益。我們也對零售業務的投資感興趣（例如 Catalyst Brands LLC）；一家電子商務企業（Rue Gil"},{"en":"As of December 31, 2024, and until October 31, 2025, we owned an 88% noncontrolling interest in The Taubman Realty Group, LLC, or TRG. As further discussed in Note 4 to the financial statements, on October 31, 2025, we acquired the remaining 12% interest which we did not previously own, or the TRG Acquisition.","zh":"截至 2024 年 12 月 31 日，直至 2025 年 10 月 31 日，我們擁有 The Taubman Realty Group, LLC 或 TRG 88% 的非控制權益。正如財務報表附註 4 中進一步討論的，2025 年 10 月 31 日，我們收購了我們之前未擁有的剩餘 12% 權益，即 TRG 收購。"}],"markets":[],"customers":[],"competition":[{"en":"The retail real estate industry is dynamic and competitive. We compete with numerous merchandise distribution channels, including malls, outlet centers, community/lifestyle centers, and other shopping centers in the United States and abroad. We also compete with internet retailing sites and catalogs, including our tenants, which provide retailers with distribution options beyond existing brick and mortar retail properties. The existence of competitive alternatives could have a material adverse effect on our ability to lease space and on the level of rents we can obtain. This results in competition for both the tenants to occupy the properties that we develop and manage as well as for the acquisition of prime sites (including land for development and operating properties). We believe that there are numerous factors that make our properties highly desirable to retailers, including:","zh":"零售房地產行業充滿活力且競爭激烈。我們與眾多商品分銷管道競爭，包括美國和國外的購物中心、直銷中心、社區/生活方式中心以及其他購物中心。我們也與網路零售網站和目錄競爭，包括我們的租戶，它們為零售商提供了現有實體零售物業以外的分銷選擇。競爭性替代方案的存在可能會對我們租賃空間的能力和我們可以獲得的租金水平產生重大不利影響。這導致租戶爭奪我們開發和管理的物業以及收購黃金地段（包括用於開發和經營物業的土地）。我們相信，有許多因素使我們的房產受到零售商的青睞，包括："},{"en":"issued 820,977 restricted shares of Simon common stock and 724,222 long-term incentive performance units, or LTIP units, net of forfeitures, under the Simon Property Group, L.P. 2019 Stock Incentive Plan, or the 2019 Plan;","zh":"根據 Simon Property Group, L.P. 2019 年股票激勵計劃或 2019 年計劃，發行 820,977 股西蒙普通股限制性股票和 724,222 股長期激勵績效單位或 LTIP 單位（扣除沒收後）；"}],"segments":{},"peers":["PLD","PSA","BXP","VNO","VMRK"]}}